# BeetleCraft

BeetleBoy running on ComputerCraft.

Claim your Universal Basic Cheese, Hunt Beetles, Showcase Remilia profiles, and chat with other angels.

Requires a monitor peripheral (falls back to term).
User cards displayed on the homepage are listed in `users.txt`, one username per line.

## Install

In the ComputerCraft terminal:
```
wget run https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<user>/<repo>/main/beetlecraft/installer/install.lua
```

This downloads all files and recreates the directory structure. Run `cd beetlecraft && main` to start.

To regenerate the installer after changing files:
```
python3 installer/build.py --repo <user>/<repo>
```

## Auth

Tokens live in `.env` (auto-created on first run).
Ships with a shared account (Echoes of MiladyCraft); edit the file to use your own:

```
REFRESH_TOKEN=<your_token>
```

## Dependencies

Connects to `cdn.goulag.dev` for PNG-to-NFP image conversion (avatar rendering and chat images). 
Connects to `remistats.net`to get user global/project ranks.

## Structure

```
main.lua            Entry point and main loop
lib/auth.lua        Token storage, refresh, authenticated requests
lib/reminet.lua     All HTTP calls (profiles, beetles, images)
lib/chat_ws.lua     Native WebSocket client for miladychan shoutbox
lib/ui.lua          Drawing primitives and hit testing
lib/utils.lua       Persistence, palette, formatting
scenes/             One file per screen (home, profile, beetleboy, chat)
assets/             Beetle sprites (png and nfp) & splash screen nfp
```
